# Byte-exact evidence files.
#
# evidence/preregistration.json is an evidence artifact, not source. Its SHA-256 is attested inside
# evidence/meta.json and quoted in the published report, and it was frozen with CRLF line endings.
# With core.autocrlf=true, git rewrites it to LF when committing and back to CRLF when checking out,
# so a clone on macOS or Linux would hash it differently and the published hash would not verify.
# `-text` disables every end-of-line conversion for this path: the bytes are stored and checked out
# exactly as they are, on every platform.
evidence/preregistration.json -text
